Entry point File Use it when <code>&lt;vexy-stax&gt;</code> Web Component <code>vexy-stax.element.js</code> You want markup only, no JavaScript ES module: <code>createStax</code>, <code>VexyStax</code> <code>vexy-stax.element.js</code> or the npm package You script the deck Global script: <code>window.VexyStax</code> <code>vexy-stax.global.js</code> You load a classic <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> without modules <p>The smallest working page needs one script tag and one element:</p> <pre><code>&lt;script type="module" src="https://vexy.dev/vexy-stax-js/vexy-stax.element.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;vexy-stax slides="layer-0.png layer-1.png layer-2.png" view="compact"&gt;&lt;/vexy-stax&gt;
</code></pre> <p>The element builds a scene from the image list, renders it in the compact view, and toggles between compact and expanded when you click it. See the Quickstart.</p>

Attribute Value Effect <code>slides</code> Image URLs separated by spaces or newlines Builds a scene with <code>makeScene</code>. The first URL is the backmost plate. <code>captions</code> <code>true</code> or <code>false</code> With <code>slides</code> only: the global <code>captions</code> setting of the built scene <code>scene</code> URL of a <code>.scene.json</code> file Fetches and parses the scene <code>config</code> Scene as a JSON string Inline scene; read once when the element connects <p>A child <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> holds a full scene without attribute escaping:</p> <pre><code>&lt;vexy-stax view="compact" aspect="3"&gt;
  &lt;script type="application/json"&gt;
  {
    "version": 1,
    "transition": { "kind": "expand_collapse" },
    "slides": [
      { "src": "https://example.com/layer-0.png", "caption": { "text": "First layer" } },
      { "src": "https://example.com/layer-1.png" }
    ]
  }
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/vexy-stax&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Invalid JSON in that child fails the mount with <code>&lt;vexy-stax&gt;: inline &lt;script&gt; scene is not valid JSON (…)</code>.</p>
